Third-party material: CQ's WAZ Zone Definitions
-----------------------------------------------

The file(s) src/cq_zones_mcp/data/published/cq_waz_list.htm
is CQ's "WAZ Zone Definitions" page (https://cqww.com/cq_waz_list.htm, "Updated and correct
as of April 1, 2018"), copyright CQ Communications, Inc. and the World Wide Radio Operators
Foundation, Inc. (WWROF), all rights reserved. It is shipped unmodified; data/SOURCE.json records
its SHA-256 and a test checks the file against it.

data/facts/cq_zones.json holds facts from that page (zone numbers, names, and the entities and
areas each zone covers, in CQ's own words), each citing the zone it comes from, so the tools can
answer from CQ's definitions. The definitions are CQ's and WWROF's, not ours.

This project's GPL-3.0-or-later licence covers our own code and files. It does not cover the
owner's published file(s) or the facts from them, and we claim no rights in them.

Ours: everything else in data/, which is our arrangement of the owner's facts and is labelled as
ours: data/SOURCE.json, data/owner-list.schema.json, data/derived/ (built from the facts) and
data/load.sql (generated).

Test material: tests/crosscheck/cty.dat is AD1C's country file (https://www.country-files.com/),
MIT licence, with its notice in tests/crosscheck/AD1C-LICENSE.txt. It is used only as a cross-check
in the tests and is not part of the published package.
